cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite them as below."
title: "Memory X-Ray: Do an LLM's self-reported evidence citations match the evidence that drives its decisions?"
abstract: >-
  A controlled evidence-ablation study of Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct. In six scenarios (three designed
  controls and three synthetic macro-finance cases), every subset of four evidence records is shown in
  three fixed orderings (48 deterministic prompts per scenario), label probabilities are scored, and exact
  Shapley values, leave-one-out, necessity and sufficiency are computed. The model's self-reported
  citations are then tested against these behavioral attributions. Attributions are behavioral, not
  mechanistic; results are case studies of six scenarios with one model.
type: software
